+## Revision 2 (2026-10-13): the compliance officer's edit
+
+The compliance system gained one rule, R7 `connected_exposure_cap`: connected exposure (the principal of
+every open facility at businesses an owner holds 25% or more of) over $250,000 always goes to a human.
+It was added to `compliance.json` and `policy.md` and imported with `loan import --rules-only`; the
+bank's policy engine (`loan policy`) now reports it with effect `human`. Revision 1 of this procedure
+would see R7 in `fired` and still file. Revision 2 changes one thing: `precedents.py` sets
+`needs_human` when any fired rule has effect `human`, so `by-confidence` ends the run unfiled with a
+note for the human. The judgment step still runs first (the policy band is review), so the human
+reads the typed answers alongside the figures. Frontmatter `version` is "2"; nothing else moved.
